# Staging host keys for the CD deploy job (.github/workflows/cd.yml).
#
# This file is committed on purpose: the deploy refuses to disable host-key
# checking, so the runner has to be told which key the staging box presents.
# A host key is a public value -- there is nothing secret in it.
#
# Populate it with the real staging host, once, and commit the result:
#
#   ssh-keyscan -p 22 staging.example.com > deploy/staging_known_hosts
#   ssh-keygen -lf deploy/staging_known_hosts      # note the fingerprint
#
# Verify that fingerprint out of band (the provider's console) before committing
# it: `ssh-keyscan` returns whatever answers on port 22, which is exactly what an
# active man-in-the-middle would want you to trust.
#
# The file is currently unpopulated on purpose -- the staging host has not been
# provisioned yet. The deploy job detects this and fails with the ssh-keyscan
# command above rather than connecting with verification switched off.
#
# A valid entry is one line: "<host> ssh-ed25519 AAAA...". The guard in cd.yml
# matches the key type after the hostname, not at the start of the line.
